/// A conversion the compiler makes on its own, where an argument of this type is passed to
/// a parameter of type `T` (spec §7.2, §7.6): `rl::DrawText(name, …)` with a `String`
/// `name`, where `DrawText` takes a `cstr`, calls `convert` on it.
///
/// Only arguments convert, never a `let`, a field or a `return`, so whatever `convert`
/// borrows is used by the call and not kept past it. The argument is borrowed, not moved;
/// one conversion is made at most, never two in a row; and none is tried to choose
/// between a C++ overload set's members or to infer a generic parameter.
///
/// It is written by the module that declares the type converted from, or the type
/// converted to: `impl ImplicitAs<Vec2> for rl::Vector2` belongs with `Vec2`. A plain
/// method never converts on its own.
pub trait ImplicitAs<T> {
    fn convert(&self) -> T
}
